+# Codebase Audit — Enterprise Readiness
+
+Date: 2026-08-14
+Scope: `leish_v2` frontend (Next.js 16 / React 19 / TypeScript / Tailwind 4)
+
+## Verdict
+
+The codebase is **solid for a production-bound frontend demo** and now meets the
+baseline for enterprise delivery: strict TypeScript, zero lint warnings, a committed
+lockfile, no known vulnerabilities, unit tests, CI, security headers, SEO, and
+accessibility fixes. Remaining gaps are architectural (backend/data layer), not code
+hygiene.
+
+---
+
+## What was already strong
+
+| Area                         | Status                                                                                      |
+| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| TypeScript `strict` mode     | ✅ on                                                                                       |
+| Lint / typecheck             | ✅ clean (0 errors, 0 warnings)                                                             |
+| `npm audit`                  | ✅ 0 vulnerabilities                                                                        |
+| Lockfile committed           | ✅ `package-lock.json` (v3)                                                                 |
+| React Strict Mode            | ✅ default in Next 16                                                                       |
+| Hydration safety             | ✅ `useSyncExternalStore` for auth/theme; `suppressHydrationWarning` on `<html>`            |
+| Server/client boundaries     | ✅ client components colocated with `"use client"`, server pages use `generateStaticParams` |
+| No `any` in application code | ✅ (1 occurrence is a comment)                                                              |
+
+## Gaps found & fixed this pass
+
+### 1. Testing (added)
+
+- **Before:** zero tests.
+- **After:** Vitest + React Testing Library + jest-dom + user-event.
+  - 22 tests across `src/lib/artists.test.ts` (filter logic), `src/lib/utils.test.ts`,
+    `src/components/Button.test.tsx`, `src/components/RatingStars.test.tsx`.
+  - Filter logic extracted from the page into a pure function `filterArtists`
+    (`src/lib/artists.ts`) — deterministic and unit-testable.
+  - Scripts: `npm test`, `npm run test:watch`, `npm run test:coverage`.
+  - Config: `vitest.config.mts`, `vitest.setup.ts`.
+
+### 2. CI/CD (added)
+
+- `.github/workflows/ci.yml`: `npm ci` → lint → typecheck → test → build on every PR
+  and push to `main`. (Push must happen from a new session — remote access is closed.)
+
+### 3. Security (added)
+
+- `next.config.ts`:
+  - `poweredByHeader: false` (removes `X-Powered-By`).
+  - Production-only security headers, verified live:
+    `X-Frame-Options: DENY`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`,
+    `Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin`,
+    `Permissions-Policy`, `Strict-Transport-Security`, and a `Content-Security-Policy`
+    (`default-src 'self'`, `object-src 'none'`, `frame-ancestors 'none'`, …).
+    Dev is exempt so HMR keeps working.
+  - `validateEnv()` fail-fast pattern (`src/env.mjs`); `.env.example` documents
+    `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL`.
+- No secrets in the repo; `.env*` gitignored (verified).
+
+### 4. SEO & metadata (added)
+
+- `src/app/robots.ts` (blocks private routes, references sitemap).
+- `src/app/sitemap.ts` (static routes + all artist/studio profiles).
+- `metadataBase`, `openGraph`, `twitter` card in `src/app/layout.tsx`.
+- `viewport` export with `themeColor` matching the brand header.
+
+### 5. Resilience (added)
+
+- `src/app/error.tsx` — route-level error boundary; deliberately does **not** render
+  `error.message` (leaks internals); logs to console for an error tracker.
+- `src/app/loading.tsx` — accessible route-level loading state (`role="status"`).
+
+### 6. Accessibility (fixed)
+
+- **Forms:** added real `<label htmlFor>` + `id` + `name` + `autoComplete` to login,
+  register, forgot-password, onboarding, and booking forms (previously
+  placeholder-only labels — an a11y violation).
+- **Artists page:** `aria-pressed` on toggle chips, `aria-live="polite"` on the
+  results count, `fieldset`/`legend` for event filters, sr-only labels for selects,
+  removed the dead no-op "Filter" button.
+- **Errors:** `role="alert"` on form error messages.
+
+### 7. Performance
+
+- Removed `unoptimized` from the header logo — Next.js now serves optimized
+  (WebP/AVIF) versions via its image pipeline (sharp is present as a dependency).
+- All other images already used `next/image` with `sizes` and lazy loading.
+
+## Round 2 — architectural upgrades (completed)
+
+Follow-up pass converting the frontend demo into a real client-server app:
+
+| Item             | Delivered                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |
+| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| **Persistence**  | better-sqlite3 with WAL + startup migrations (`src/server/db.ts`), `data/leish.db` gitignored; repository surface designed so Prisma/PostgreSQL can replace it without touching callers                                                                                                                                     |
+| **Real auth**    | `POST /api/auth/register\|login\|logout`, `GET /api/auth/me`; passwords hashed with Node `crypto.scrypt` (per-user salt, timing-safe compare); stateless JWT sessions in httpOnly, sameSite=lax cookies; middleware protects `/dashboard`, `/onboarding`, `/api/bookings`; pages wired to the API with loading/error states |
+| **Bookings API** | `GET/POST /api/bookings` — auth required, zod-validated, **price resolved server-side from the catalog** (client can't set pricing); dashboard lists real bookings from SQLite                                                                                                                                              |
+| **Catalog API**  | `GET /api/artists` — public, zod-validated filters reusing `filterArtists()`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |
+| **Validation**   | zod schemas for all request bodies/queries (`src/server/validation.ts`), unit-tested                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |
+| **Formatting**   | Prettier (`format` / `format:check`, CI gate), applied repo-wide                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |
+| **Tests**        | 39 tests (17 new): scrypt hashing, JWT sign/verify/tamper, zod schemas + existing filters/components                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |
+
+## Round 3 — auth hardening & observability (completed)
+
+| Item                      | Delivered                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |
+| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
+| **Rate limiting**         | In-memory sliding-window limiter (`src/server/ratelimit.ts`) keyed by client IP (x-forwarded-for aware), applied to login (10/min), register (10/min), forgot-password (5/min), reset-password (10/min); 429 + Retry-After; idle-bucket sweeper; unit-tested                                                                                                                                                                                                       |
+| **Password reset (real)** | `POST /api/auth/forgot-password` — single-use 1-hour token; only a sha256 hash stored (`password_resets` table), raw token never persisted; generic response (no user enumeration); dev mode surfaces the reset link (no email provider in sandbox — production hooks Resend/SES here). `POST /api/auth/reset-password` — validates token, sets new scrypt hash, invalidates outstanding tokens. `/reset-password` page added; `/forgot-password` wired to the API |
+| **Structured logging**    | pino + pino-pretty (`src/server/logger.ts`), `LOG_LEVEL` env; security events logged (failed login, reset issuance/completion, rate-limit hits); JSON in prod, pretty in dev                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |
+| **E2E (Playwright)**      | `e2e/journey.spec.ts` — register → book → dashboard + protected-route redirect; `playwright.config.ts` (chromium, CI reporter, artifact upload); dedicated CI job with browser install. Note: sandbox blocks the browser CDN, so e2e runs in GitHub Actions only                                                                                                                                                                                                   |
+| **Dependency pinning**    | `package.json` now uses exact versions (no `^`/`~`) for runtime deps; lockfile v3                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  |
+| **Shared HTTP helpers**   | `src/server/http.ts` — consistent `jsonError`, `enforceRateLimit`, `readJson` (discriminated union) used by all API routes                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |
+| **Tests**                 | 48 total (9 new: rate limiter, reset tokens)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |
+
+Verified end-to-end with curl: reset link issued → password updated → token single-use (400 on reuse) → old password rejected / new accepted → unknown email leaks nothing → 15 rapid logins → 429.
+
+## Round 4 — email verification & nonce CSP (completed)
+
+| Item                   | Delivered                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |
+| ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| **Email service**      | `src/server/email.ts` — provider abstraction: `dev` (default; stores in `email_outbox`, viewable at `/dev/emails` in dev builds) and `resend` (Resend API; `EMAIL_PROVIDER=resend`, `RESEND_API_KEY`, `EMAIL_FROM`; falls back to dev with a warning if misconfigured)                                                                                                                                                                                                       |
